@startuml scheduling-service-class-diagram
title Level 3: Code - Class Diagram (scheduling-service) - FR-07\nOwner: Yomna Mohamed Fekry
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
  BackgroundColor<<component>> #D5EFE0
  BorderColor<<component>> #2E8B57
}
skinparam interface {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide empty members

legend right
  |<#D5EFE0>   | Class of a component |
  |<#FFFFFF>   | Interface / domain class |
  | Solid arrow, open head | Uses (required interface / class) |
  | Dotted arrow, hollow head | Implements (provided interface) |
  | Filled diamond | Composition |
  | Plain line | Association |
endlegend

interface IScheduling <<provided>> {
  +scheduleTasks(studentId): Schedule
  +getConflicts(studentId): List<Conflict>
  +suggestSlots(taskId): List<TimeSlot>
  +moveTask(taskId, slot): void
  +markDone(taskId, done): void
  +getScheduledTasks(studentId, range): List<ScheduledTask>
}

class SchedulingService <<component>> {
  -goalPlanner: IGoalPlanner
  -assessment: IAssessment
  -studentProfile: IStudentProfile
  -repository: IScheduledTaskRepository
  -dependencyOrderer: DependencyOrderer
  -conflictDetector: ConflictDetector
  -slotFinder: SlotFinder
  --
  +scheduleTasks(...) / getConflicts(...)
  +suggestSlots(...) / moveTask(...)
  +markDone(...) / getScheduledTasks(...)
}

IScheduling <|.. SchedulingService
class DependencyOrderer <<component>> {
  +order(tasks): List<Task>
}
SchedulingService --> DependencyOrderer
class ConflictDetector <<component>> {
  +detect(tasks): List<Conflict>
}
SchedulingService --> ConflictDetector
class SlotFinder <<component>> {
  +findFree(task, slots): List<TimeSlot>
}
SchedulingService --> SlotFinder

interface IGoalPlanner <<required - Goal planner service>> {
  +generatePlan(studentId, goalText): PlanDraft
  +updateDraft(draftId, edits): PlanDraft
  +approve(draftId): Plan
  +discard(draftId): void
  +getTasks(goalId): List<PlanTask>
}

SchedulingService --> IGoalPlanner
interface IAssessment <<required - Assessment service>> {
  +addAssignment(data): Assignment
  +addExam(data): Exam
  +setStatus(assignmentId, status): void
  +setExamReminder(examId, daysBefore): void
  +getDeadlines(studentId, days): List<Deadline>
}

SchedulingService --> IAssessment
interface IStudentProfile <<required - Student service>> {
  +createProfile(studentId, data): Profile
  +updateProfile(studentId, data): Profile
  +getProfile(studentId): Profile
  +getAvailability(studentId): List<TimeSlot>
}

SchedulingService --> IStudentProfile
interface IScheduledTaskRepository <<required - Database>> {
  +save(item: ScheduledTask): void
  +findById(id): ScheduledTask
  +findByOwner(ownerId): List<ScheduledTask>
}

SchedulingService --> IScheduledTaskRepository
class ScheduledTask {
  -taskId: String
  -goalId: String
  -slot: TimeSlot
  -durationHours: int
  -done: boolean
  -status: String
  --
  +isLate(): boolean
}
class Conflict {
  -taskA: String
  -taskB: String
}
IScheduledTaskRepository --> ScheduledTask
ScheduledTask ..> Conflict
note bottom of SchedulingService
SOLID applied:
S - SchedulingService only coordinates; DependencyOrderer, ConflictDetector, SlotFinder each do one job.
O - new behaviour is added by new implementations, not by editing SchedulingService.
L - SchedulingService can replace any other IScheduling implementation.
I - IScheduling has only the operations its clients use.
D - SchedulingService depends on interfaces (IGoalPlanner, IAssessment, IStudentProfile, IScheduledTaskRepository), not on concrete classes.
end note
@enduml
